A basic game loop in C++ looks something like this:

```cpp
int main() {
    while (true) {
        // Update logic here
        render();
        handle input();
        update();
    }
}
```

That's it. You can add more complexity by adding AI, physics, or networking. The key is to keep it simple enough that you can understand the core mechanics without getting bogged down in details.
